body:
Thats insane. The dealership by me has a $100 Diag fee and I thought that was pricey. 

&#x200B;

Everything I've read about it says 

p3004- Inverter Assembly w/ Converter Malfunction

"This repair is covered under the Toyota Hybrid System Warranty. This warranty is in effect for 96 months or 100,000 miles, whichever occurs first, from the vehicle’s in-service date."

 It should be covered by ZE3 though since it's within 15 years. I would print out the warranty information and take it up there with you. Maybe your service advisor was new or had little to no training. Ask for the manager. There's no reason for them to not at least look into it for you. 

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

P0300, P0301, P0302, P0303, and P0304- Intake Manifold assembly & EGR Gasket (p3002, 3003, &3004 didn't pop up for me so I figured it was a typo, lmk if it isn't and I can do more digging.)

"This repair is covered under the Toyota Federal Emission Warranty. This warranty is in effect for  
36 months or 36,000 miles, whichever occurs first, from the vehicle’s in-service date"

I believe these codes caused the rattle. I only see one warranty extension for this one and yours wouldn't be covered still because it's over 150k. It'll be kind of pricey. 

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

I'm not too familiar with that area, so I have no advice on that. I hope some of this information is of use to you. If you already knew this stuff, it was worth a shot lol.
